# Prople Store — Feed Algorithm, Category Indexing & Scaling Blueprint

This document tracks architectural updates and algorithmic optimizations implemented across Prople Store's catalog pipeline, Home showcase generation, Category indexing, routing persistence, and search/recommendation freshness.

## 1. Firestore Timestamp Normalization & Full Catalog Sync
- **Server REST Adapter (`/api/apps.ts`)**:
  - Upgraded `parseFirestoreField` to recursively parse `timestampValue`, `mapValue`, `nullValue`, and nested `arrayValue` fields returned by the Firestore REST API.
  - Preserved Firestore document metadata (`doc.createTime` and `doc.updateTime`) as fallbacks for `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, and expanded query pagination (`?pageSize=500`) so newly published apps are never truncated or missing recency metadata.
- **Realtime Client Listener (`/src/services/firestoreAppService.ts` & `/src/context/StoreConfigContext.tsx`)**:
  - Normalized Firestore `Timestamp` instances (`toMillis()` / `{ seconds, nanoseconds }`) into deterministic numeric timestamps or ISO strings.
  - Synced `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `releaseDate`, `initialReleaseDate`, `slug`, `isIndie`, and `isPublished` into `allAppListings` so every feed surface (Home, Explore, Categories, Top Charts, Latest Releases) receives identical metadata.

## 2. Home Showcase Section Generation (`/src/utils/productionFeedAlgorithm.ts`)
- **Strict Unique ID Deduplication**:
  - Replaced lowercase app-name deduplication with strict `app.id` deduplication (`seenIds`). Distinct apps or multi-edition releases sharing a display name are no longer dropped from Home showcases.
- **Icon-Optional Eligibility**:
  - Removed the hard `iconUrl` exclusion filter in `generateProductionHomeFeed` so newly published apps using fallback monogram icons appear immediately on Home shelves.
- **Cold-Start & New Release Surfacing**:
  - Added a high-priority `New & updated releases` (`section-indie-cold-start`) showcase shelf sorted by parsed `updatedAt` / `createdAt` / `releaseDate` descending.
  - Lowered category and cold-start shelf thresholds (`minRequired = 1`) and dynamically scaled `MAX_APPEARANCES_PER_APP` for emerging catalogs so single-app categories and newly published releases reliably generate showcase sections without starving downstream shelves.
- **Freshness Boost in Personalized Ranking (`/src/services/recommendationService.ts`)**:
  - Added time-decay freshness boosts (`+35` points within 14 days, `+20` points within 45 days) using normalized timestamp parsing so newly published apps surface prominently in `Recommended for you`.

## 3. Canonical Category Indexing (`/src/components/CategoriesPage.tsx` & `/src/components/TopCharts.tsx`)
- **Eliminated Substring False Positives**:
  - Replaced broad description substring keyword matching with `doesAppMatchCategory` and `canonicalizeCategoryKey`, ensuring apps only appear under their true assigned category and explicit category tags.
- **Dynamic Custom Category Discovery & URL Slug Resolution**:
  - Merged custom categories from published apps into `CategoriesPage` and `TopCharts` filter chips, and mapped URL slugs (`/categories/:slug`) back to canonical category names on hard browser reloads.

## 4. Browser Refresh Routing & Unified Loading States
- **Solid Refresh Route Preservation (`/src/context/NavigationContext.tsx` & `/src/components/AppConsole.tsx`)**:
  - Removed the `localStorage.getItem('prople_publish_form_open')` override from `getInitialNavigationState()` and ensured `prople_publish_form_open` / `prople_publish_form_session` are cleared whenever exiting unchanged or empty publish sessions, keeping browser refreshes anchored to the active URL pathname.
- **Unified `StoreCircleLoader` Reuse**:
  - Reused the existing `StoreCircleLoader` (`SearchResultsPage` spinner) across `AppConsole` (`/studio`), `CategoriesPage`, `TopCharts`, `YouPage`, `WishlistPage`, `NotificationsPage`, `EditProfilePage`, and `RatingsAndReviewsPage` during initial auth and Firestore catalog hydration.

## 5. CI/CD Pipeline Maintenance & Lockfile-Resilient Caching (`/.github/workflows/ci.yml`)
- **Decoupled npm Cache from Strict Lockfile Presence**:
  - Removed `cache: 'npm'` from `actions/setup-node`, which previously caused immediate 6–9s job failures (`Dependencies lock file is not found`) whenever automated repository exports omitted `package-lock.json`.
  - Replaced with `actions/cache@v5` targeting `~/.npm` and keyed on `hashFiles('package-lock.json', 'package.json')`, preserving fast dependency cache hits regardless of whether `package-lock.json` is committed.
- **Node 24 Action Runtime Alignment & Hygiene**:
  - Upgraded `actions/checkout` and `actions/setup-node` to `v6` (`node24` runner runtime) to eliminate GitHub Actions Node 20 deprecation warnings, added `npm run test:catalog` verification into CI, and excluded `public/assets/aistudio/` from git tracking and PWA Workbox precaching.
